  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "J00aIbcfiQzlN6SvjQUHorv+MRk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:28.280Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "cbs Corporate Business Solutions was previously listed as independent and is not: Materna has wholly owned it since 2005. The correction lowered its receptivity score, because independence was part of why it looked receptive in the first place.\n\nWhat survives the correction is the capability claim \u2014 the strongest manufacturing bench in Germany in this set \u2014 and what qualifies it is now doubly constrained. The delivery is SAP-led and the firm is group-controlled, so an SAP-centred practice inside a parent group has two layers of technology direction set above any individual engagement.\n\nThe value of this entry is partly methodological. An ownership fact more than twenty years old had been carried in the workbook as its opposite, and checking it changed the score. Ownership is cheap to verify and expensive to get wrong, which argues for verifying it before ranking a firm on independence rather than after.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- cbs Corporate Business Solutions (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> CORRECTED: previously listed as Independent - it is a wholly owned Materna subsidiary since 2005. Receptivity score reduced. Strongest manufacturing bench in DE but SAP-led and group-controlled.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:28.280251Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:28.280256Z"
    }
  },
